xt-body","children":"Anxiety is the body preparing for a threat that has not arrived. That preparation is not imaginary — the heart really does beat faster, the chest really does tighten, thinking really does narrow. What is inaccurate is the size of the threat, not the sensation."}],"$L20"],"$L21"]}]}]]}],"$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29"]}]]}]
