20:["$","p","Roughly one in five adults lives with an anxiety condition in any given year. It is the most common and most treatable group of mental health conditions, and most people improve substantially with 8–16 weeks of structured therapy.",{"className":"text-base leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Roughly one in five adults lives with an anxiety condition in any given year. It is the most common and most treatable group of mental health conditions, and most people improve substantially with 8–16 weeks of structured therapy."}]
21:["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xl text-ink","children":"Symptom mechanics"}],[["$","p","The amygdala flags something as dangerous and triggers a surge of adrenaline before the thinking brain has weighed in. Blood is redirected to large muscles, breathing quickens to load oxygen, and digestion slows. This is why anxiety so often shows up as nausea, cold hands, or a racing pulse.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"The amygdala flags something as dangerous and triggers a surge of adrenaline before the thinking brain has weighed in. Blood is redirected to large muscles, breathing quickens to load oxygen, and digestion slows. This is why anxiety so often shows up as nausea, cold hands, or a racing pulse."}],["$","p","A panic attack is that surge at full volume. It peaks around ten minutes and cannot physically sustain itself — the body runs out of adrenaline. Knowing the ceiling exists is itself a form of relief: the sensation is intense, self-limiting, and not dangerous.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"A panic attack is that surge at full volume. It peaks around ten minutes and cannot physically sustain itself — the body runs out of adrenaline. Knowing the ceiling exists is itself a form of relief: the sensation is intense, self-limiting, and not dangerous."}]]]}]
